---
import Case from '../Case.astro';
import Shot from '../Shot.astro';
import lodge from '../../assets/shots/wickwing-lodge.webp';

const play = 'https://officialprotondev.github.io/play-wickwing/';

const facts = [
  { k: 'Role', v: 'Design and code' },
  { k: 'Built with', v: 'JavaScript and HTML canvas' },
  { k: 'Play', v: 'In your browser', href: play },
];
---

<Case id="wickwing" name="Wickwing" line="A lamplighter’s platformer you can play in the browser." facts={facts} t0={24.5} t1={25.25}>
  <div class="wrap ww-grid">
    <div class="ww-shot">
      <Shot
        src={lodge}
        alt="Wickwing’s prologue, The Lodge: a moth carrying a lantern beside a stone cottage at sundown on Emberfall Moor."
        sizes="(min-width: 90rem) 52rem, (min-width: 48rem) 60vw, 100vw"
        widths={[640, 960, 1280, 1920, 2560]}
        pixel
      />
    </div>
    <div class="ww-text">
      <p class="lede">Every autumn, the moths cross the Stillsea by the light of the Beacon.</p>
      <p>
        Wickwing is the climb to keep it lit: a pixel-art platformer where you carry a lantern up a mountain, blinking
        to braziers, burning through thickets and lighting lamps to open the way.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each room has one idea. It’s shown once somewhere safe, then asked for again where a mistake costs more, and the
        place itself explains the layout. A level lab is built in for making new rooms.
      </p>
      <p class="cta"><a href={play}>Play Wickwing</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Case>
